  "worker_cancel_during_blocked_output": true,
  "discovered_lifetime_fix": "Queued response references retained the request interrupt closure and local HTTP stream after I/O finished. Clearing the closure on the request thread closes the local socket promptly even while the router is not reading. The regression cancels a 64 MiB local upload and a second pending request before draining any router output, then verifies another response on the same connection.",
  "test_timeout_correction": "Removed a duplicate 30-second CTest override of the intended 60-second worker_tunnel timeout. Initial timeout and subsequent cancellation regression failure were retained in proof logs.",
